    "title": "CBSE Class 10th Result 2026 Highlights: Register for 2nd chance exams, pay fees",
    "text": "CBSE 10th Result 2026 Live: Students can check thier Cbse 10th result at cbse.gov.in, results.cbse.gov.inCBSE Class 10th Result 2026 Live Updates: The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) Class 10th results are declared on April 15. Students can access the results at the official websites — results.cbse.nic.in, cbseresults.nic.in, cbse.gov.in. Nearly 25 lakh students appeared for their exams. Among schools, Kendriya Vidalayas scored the highest pass percentage at 99.57%. Students who have passed the main Class 10 exams can opt to improve their performance in up to three subjects, including science, mathematics, social science, and languages. Registrations begin today. CBSE 10th Result 2026 LIVE: Check HereThe overall pass percentage in CBSE Class 10 (full subjects) saw a marginal improvement in 2026 compared to the previous year. In its notice shared on X (formerly Twitter), the platform announced that the results will be announced shortly, advising the students to set up their accounts on the cloud platform. For more details on CBSE Class 10 and 12 results, students can check IE Education. CBSE Class 10th Result 2026 Update This year, the CBSE Class 10 exams are being conducted under the two-board system, which involves two separate examination sessions. We spoke to teachers, students, and parents on the two-board examination system and here’s what they say. CBSE Class 10th Result 2026: Know where and how to check marks – cbse.nic.in, Digilocker, Umang app, IVRS As per data by the board, as many as 25,08,319 students were to appear for the exams this year. Out of them, 14,08,546 were male, and 10,99,773 were female. The Class 10 exams were organised for 83 subjects across 8,075 exam centres. Check the IE Education portal for latest updates on CBSE 10th board results. (Representative Image/AI) Class 10th Result CBSE 2026 Live Updates: In order to access their scores, students will need to enter their roll number, date of birth, and other necessary information. The Class 10 exams were held between February 17 and March 11, 2026, commencing with the Mathematics Standard paper. All examinations were conducted in a single shift, beginning at 10:30 am. © IE Online Media Services Pvt LtdThis article was first uploaded on April fourteenth, twenty twenty-six, at thirty-six minutes past ten in the morning. Tags: Board exams 2026 CBSE CBSE 10th Results Class 10 results Class X Class X board examination class X exams Class X results",
